WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.627
The teaching database includes several examples because reshaping appears in many domains.

00:00:05.627 --> 00:00:08.602
Admissions and sales begin in long form.

00:00:08.602 --> 00:00:12.192
Monthly sales and patient metrics begin in wide form.

00:00:12.192 --> 00:00:16.417
Survey responses and grades are useful for matrix-style pivots.

00:00:16.417 --> 00:00:22.242
The different examples help you focus on the reshape pattern rather than memorizing one dataset.

00:00:22.242 --> 00:00:28.752
Connect this idea to a machine-learning workflow converting wide measurements into tidy long data.

00:00:28.752 --> 00:00:34.212
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:34.212 --> 00:00:41.767
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:41.767 --> 00:00:47.477
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:47.477 --> 00:00:53.120
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
